From: Martin Jungblut Schreiner <martin.schreiner@suse.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lxml: point setup.py install at the internal libxml2/libxslt too

Only "setup.py build" is told where the internal xml2-config/xslt-config
live. lxml reads those options on every invocation, and without them
"setup.py install" falls back to pkg-config and then xml2-config on PATH.
With an internal Python and an internal libxml2/libxslt, and no libxml2
development package installed, that fails:

  Error: Please make sure the libxml2 and libxslt development packages are installed.

Pass the same options to the install step. No change with a system
libxml2/libxslt, where both expand to nothing.

--- a/external/lxml/ExternalProject_lxml.mk
+++ b/external/lxml/ExternalProject_lxml.mk
@@ -38,6 +38,8 @@
 		rm -fr install && \
 		mkdir install && \
 		$(lxml_PYTHON) -Wi setup.py install \
+			$(if $(SYSTEM_LIBXML),,--with-xml2-config=$(gb_UnpackedTarball_workdir)/libxml2/xml2-config) \
+			$(if $(SYSTEM_LIBXSLT),,--with-xslt-config=$(gb_UnpackedTarball_workdir)/libxslt/xslt-config) \
 			--install-lib install \
 	)
 	$(call gb_Trace_EndRange,lxml,EXTERNAL)
